PL-3 Permutation D — Refactor to eliminate the duplication entirely.

Strategy:
  `chrome.scripting.executeScript({...})` accepts an `args:` array whose
  values are JSON-serialised and passed as parameters to the injected
  `func:`. Rather than inline-duplicating the section anchors, we
  centralise them in scraper.js, import the constants in background.js,
  and pass them through `args:`.

  scraper.js continues to export `doScrape` / `parseResetMinutes` /
  `isHydrated` for unit tests. It additionally exports `SECTION_ANCHORS`
  and `EXTRA_TOGGLE_SELECTOR` — both consumed by background.js.

  background.js builds the args object at the SW-context call site
  (where ES imports work) and references the anchors via parameters
  inside the page-context `func:`.

This eliminates the parity gap PL-3 was asking us to lint. No new lint
needed; the existing regex-set lint stays in place for the regex
literals (which still have to be inlined verbatim because regex
literals are not serialisable through `args:`).

---

Sketch of the source change (illustrative, not a runnable patch):

