Caveats:
  1. background.js currently does NOT import from scraper.js — it owns a
     separate `parseResetMinutes` at the SW scope. Adding the import is
     trivial (MV3 service workers support ES modules when manifest.json
     sets `"background.type": "module"`). Verify manifest already sets
     module type or add it.
  2. Regex literals (e.g. `/^Last updated:/`) still cannot be passed via
     `args:` (JSON-serialisable values only) and must remain inlined.
     The existing regex-set lint continues to cover those.
  3. Test surface: `scraper.test.js` calls `doScrape(text, bool)`
     directly. The export of `SECTION_ANCHORS` is invisible to those
     tests; no test change required.

Effort:
  ~25 lines edited across scraper.js and background.js. One round of
  manual verification (load extension, navigate to claude.ai/settings/usage,
  confirm scrape still produces meters).
